  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (3S,7R,8Ar)-3-Benzyl-7-Hydroxyhexahydropyrrolo[1,2-A]Pyrazine-1,4-Dione and Tankyrase-2 through a series of target interactions involving SNU-387. This compound appears to act as a target for multiple molecules, including (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, S-ethylcysteine zwitterion, and 6,7-Dimethoxy-2-Methyl-3,4-Dihydroisoquinolin-1-One, all of which are known to target Tankyrase-2. The shared involvement of SNU-387 in these pathways indicates a possible mechanism of action, where the initial compound may interact with a common target, thereby influencing Tankyrase-2 activity. The evidence suggests a possible dependency on the target SNU-387, which in turn modulates Tankyrase-2 function, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated.",
